OL,3,GNEWSAPark trees to be felled after elm
OL,4,Adisease outbreak
OL,5,
OL,6,FAbout 200 trees are to be removed from
OL,7,Fa park in Brighton after an outbreak of
OL,8,Felm disease.
OL,10,FBrighton & Hove City Council said that
OL,11,Fthe work at Withdean Park was needed to
OL,12,Fhelp stop the disease spreading and
OL,13,Fprevent it recurring through
OL,14,Finterconnected root systems.
OL,16,FThe affected elms were identified
OL,17,Fduring inspections which found a
OL,18,Fsignificant outbreak in a small area of
OL,19,Fthe park, and the work is expected to
OL,20,Ftake about three weeks from Monday. A
OL,21,Fmature ash tree is also being removed.
OL,23,APub: 19-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,330,320,200,140,0,100
